    "['isis ipv6 enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-address', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis ipv6 enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-address\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 1\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. Replace `<interface-name>` with the actual interface name (e.g., `ge-1/0/0.0` or `lo0.0`)\\n2. Juniper requires explicit level configuration (level 1 in this case)\\n3. The command enables IPv6 IS-IS on the specified interface for level 1, matching the HUAWEI configuration where IS-IS level is set to level-1 (`is-level level-1`) and IPv6 IS-IS is enabled on the interface\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-address'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 1', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis ipv6 enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> ipv6-address\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 1\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. Replace `<interface-name>` with the actual interface name (e.g., `ge-1/0/0.0` or `lo0.0`)\\n2. Juniper requires explicit level configuration (level 1 in this case)\\n3. The command enables IPv6 IS-IS on the specified interface for level 1, matching the HUAWEI configuration where IS-IS level is set to level-1 (`is-level level-1`) and IPv6 IS-IS is enabled on the interface\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 1'}]]": 1,
